    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.16) and **Gunnar Henderson** (71.80), both projected for elite output against favorable matchups. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a significant 16% park factor adjustment, and despite the slight disadvantage of facing a right-hander like Chris Bassitt, his sustained recency and top-tier placement in the two-hole make him our most reliable anchor. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** faces the struggling Patrick Corbin; while the platoon disadvantage against a left-handed pitcher trims his ceiling slightly, his projected volume and park advantage in the order make him an essential play. We are also high on **Coby Mayo** (66.71), whose 8% boost from a favorable platoon setup against Corbin makes him a superior start to several other mid-tier options.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the final utility spot, where **Miguel Vargas** (62.95) narrowly missed the cut in favor of **Josh Jung** (63.10). While **Miguel Vargas** projected well due to a strong SP skill matchup against the lefty Rojas, **Josh Jung** garnered a higher score by virtue of his premium spot in the order and a favorable 19% SP skill adjustment against Spencer Arrighetti. Elsewhere, **Sam Antonacci** (46.57) remains in the lineup as a marginal start, though he carries risk due to a negative platoon split against Rojas and a low batting position. **Dominic Smith** (43.00) rounds out the outfield with a marginal score, but he carries a \u26a0\ufe0f 35% rain risk that necessitates monitoring before first pitch to ensure we aren't burning a game cap on a rain-shortened outing. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** either on the IL or enjoying an off-day, the Waves must lean heavily on the remaining core to capitalize on these specific pitching matchups.",
